{
  "rationale": "Final design: I keep the revised design from my Round-2 revision with the same geometry and controller values, and accept or partly accept each critique point as follows.\n\nKept, with reasons:\n- base_speed 1.5. The critique is right that PWM-to-ground-speed is unmeasured, so this value is still an estimate. It is the lowest speed that plausibly gives the roughly 1.5 m/s average needed for completion within 3 s, and it is below the 1.6 draft to give margin on tight bends. Its adequacy is a question for the race data, not something I claim here.\n- kp 3.5 with signal ranges of about 0.2 to 0.6 gives a turn of about 0.7 to 2.1 units (245 to 735 PWM per wheel). I accept the critique's warning that a steady high turn could cause cross-line oscillation. I keep kp at 3.5 because the rms_error decision rule can move it on evidence from the first race.\n- kd 0.15 as a light damper. The critique notes that my noise figure was asserted without a stated basis. I accept that the derivative contribution is unverified, but a small kd is the lower-risk choice whichever way the noise really is.\n- ki 0.05. The critique is correct that it is effectively inert and gives no steady-state correction. I make no claim that it does, and I keep it small rather than add an untested integral term.\n- Sensor row at y=0.06 with x from -0.04 to +0.04 in 0.02 m steps. The critique notes that lateral coverage is only roughly one or two sensors on the line up to about 0.04 m offset, and that the outer sensors may lose the line on the slalom. I accept that as a risk. I keep the layout because widening it would reduce tape resolution at the centre, and this is the first race to test it.\n- line_loss last_direction. The critique notes its sign may point the wrong way after an S-bend. I accept that as untested. I keep it because the alternatives are equally untested and the 0.35 throttle slows recovery.\n- body_width 0.12. The off-track limit is 0.06 m regardless, so the body size has no real effect here.\n\nChanged or rejected:\n- I reject the critique's suggestion of a much lower starting speed. Completion within 3 s needs real speed, and the first race is the evidence that will decide whether 1.5 is too high.\n- I accept that there is no curvature-based slowing. I do not add one, because the contract offers only constant base_pwm.\n- I acknowledge that the decision rule in my draft could cut speed when max_error exceeds 0.05 on a normal recovery. I keep the rule, but the next iteration should check line_loss_events and completion as well, not max_error alone.\n\nExpected result: completion on the oval and s-bend, with the most risk on the slalom from outer-sensor line loss and recovery direction. The next iteration should use the measured progress, line_loss_events and steering_oscillation to choose between a speed change and a kp change.",
